---
# clang-tidy configuration for urbi-embedded.
#
# The project is strict C99 with a deliberate systems-programming style.
# const-correctness is a project goal: all read-only by-value parameters
# are const-qualified in definitions (though not in prototypes, where
# top-level const is stripped by the compiler and is noise).
#
# Several clang-tidy check categories are tuned off because they target
# C++ idioms, conflict with explicit design choices, or produce noise
# that doesn't help the embedded/robotics audience:
#
# - modernize-*         : C++-focused (use auto, nullptr, range-for, ...)
# - cppcoreguidelines-* : C++ guidelines; do not apply to C
# - readability-isolate-declaration : we group related locals intentionally
# - llvm-header-guard   : we use our own ULEX_H / URBI_H style guards
#
# Three additional individual checks are disabled because they are
# famously noisy or collide with strict-C99 / embedded conventions.
# The rationale per check:
#
# - cert-err33-c : flags every call whose return value is "expected" to be
#   checked (printf family, fgets, ...).  In embedded code the prints are
#   often debug aids and ignoring the return is deliberate.
#
# - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters : flags any function with two
#   adjacent same-typed parameters as "easily swappable" without semantic
#   analysis.  Floods projects that use paired parameters like (lo, hi),
#   (src, dst), (line, col) with false positives.
#
# - readability-identifier-length : conflicts with canonical C style
#   (`i` loop index, `p` cursor, `n` count).  STYLE.md explicitly endorses
#   short names in tight scopes.
#
# - clang-diagnostic-gnu-label-as-value : fired by `&&label` and `goto *ptr`
#   in the computed-goto dispatch path of uvm.c (UVM_USE_COMPUTED_GOTO).
#   These extensions are intentional: they implement threaded dispatch and are
#   gated behind `#if defined(__GNUC__) || defined(__clang__)`, so the code
#   only activates on compilers that support the extensions.  Suppressing the
#   diagnostic here keeps clang-tidy clean without the `-Wno-gnu-*` flags
#   needed by the GCC build.
#
# - clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding : flags structs whose field
#   order leaves more than a small number of padding bytes.  UVM (and a
#   handful of other long-lived singletons) is intentionally grouped by
#   subsystem — alloc / M2-additions / scheduler / GC / watcher / counters
#   — to keep code review tractable.  UVM is a singleton; padding cost is
#   trivial vs. the readability of subsystem grouping.  Re-enable per-call
#   site (or per-struct) if a hot per-cell layout ever needs it.
#
# bugprone-*, performance-*, portability-*, and clang-analyzer-* are kept
# enabled (via clang-tidy defaults) since they catch real defects and
# apply cleanly to C.

Checks: >
  -modernize-*,
  -cppcoreguidelines-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables,
  -readability-isolate-declaration,
  -llvm-header-guard,
  -cert-err33-c,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -clang-diagnostic-gnu-label-as-value,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.performance.Padding

WarningsAsErrors: ''

HeaderFilterRegex: '^src/.*\.h$'

FormatStyle: none
